---
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
  Client-side search index. Titles come from _data/nav.yml so they match the
  sidebar exactly; bodies are the rendered page with HTML stripped. Truncated
  per page to keep the whole index a single small download.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
{%- assign pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.url contains '/tutorial/'" -%}
{%- assign emitted = 0 -%}
{%- for p in pages -%}
  {%- assign nav_title = nil -%}
  {%- assign nav_section = nil -%}
  {%- for section in site.data.nav.sections -%}
    {%- for ch in section.chapters -%}
      {%- if ch.url == p.url -%}
        {%- assign nav_title = ch.num | append: ". " | append: ch.title -%}
        {%- assign nav_section = section.title -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if p.url == '/tutorial/' -%}
    {%- assign nav_title = "Tutorial introduction" -%}
    {%- assign nav_section = "Overview" -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Comma is driven by how many entries actually got written, not by
    forloop.first: a skipped first page would otherwise emit a leading comma
    and make the whole document invalid JSON.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if nav_title -%}
    {%- if emitted > 0 %},{% endif -%}
    {
      "title": {{ nav_title | jsonify }},
      "section": {{ nav_section | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ p.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
      "body": {{ p.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncate: 6000 | jsonify }}
    }
    {%- assign emitted = emitted | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
